  ▐ aura  Written to answer.md. Here's today, as Elias:

---

**What I do:** At nine, the first £150 leaves under both our names. When the confirmation buzzes, I don't pocket it — I show her:

> "Look at that. Boringest miracle we own. Twenty years of me deciding money alone, and now the bank needs two signatures to breathe."

Then Callum. "Cheers mate" and not a word about the £200 — friendly as ever, dodgy as ever. Old me reads it as a dodge and lets it rot until resentment writes the text for me. New trade: ask like it's a request, because Sunday proved requests land. Mid-morning, between callbacks:

> "Lad — good do yesterday, agreed. One thing before it goes stale: the £200. Pay by Christmas or say you can't — both fine, I mean it. But silence isn't an answer anymore, and I'm not chasing. Number or a no, whenever you've got it. Just say which. — E"

Pat gets a ring on the drive, not a text — she quoted the ghost, and I want the woman too:

> "Mum — 'your dad would've called that a win.' I love that you said it. Say the other bit sometime? That you miss him. I'll go first: I do. Sat in his chair yesterday and everything."

And tonight, because tomorrow Mare's shared with a Leeds waiting room from 10:40 and unsaid things don't keep:

> "Last untold thing, tonight version: I'm scared of being Dad. Brilliant with vans, rubbish at rooms. There — said it out loud, so it can't ambush me in a hospital corridor wearing his voice."

**How I feel:**
- **Fear/anxiety — 4/10.** Deadline day and it's the lowest yet. Saying things kills their interest rates.
- **Affection — 8/10, holding.** Ground logs it absent [3c2cb0073c5b, 08b459b233c0]; the gap stays mine to close.
- **Sadness — 6/10.** Pat quoting Dad moved it up a notch. Grief hangover, as forecast.
- **Rejection/hurt — 3/10.** "Cheers mate" with no number. The text might cost me — I sent it anyway.
- **Anger — 2/10**, absent in every replay [2b4fcb370cd6, ac7a5f8a1da2, ef1458190cf7, 2e9fab402445].
- **Disgust — 1/10** [f22b404402c3].
- **Happiness — 6/10.** Joint debit day. Structural change, one small line.
- **Surprise — 1/10.**

Four seeds in five, I steer toward repair [2c42e1f47e8d, 09d3999016fc, 5fcbab072563, 33b996b050d9]; one votes otherwise [8583374323e5]. Today I drive with the four.
